      "message": "This looks like the reason why you need to keep the elements in `mMfcs` in order of their inactive duration. In order to keep this ordering property, current implementation need to make a new copy of `mMfcs` every time when it expires an existing entry.\n\nGiven it\u0027s unlikely that the number of MFCs can exceeds MFC_MAX_NUMBER_OF_ENTRIES, I think it\u0027s okay to just remove a random one. More importantly, the system won\u0027t be broken if an active MFC is removed here, because we will receive a new NO_CACHE up call for it and then add it back (it\u0027s also unlikely that a newly added MFC is removed and added again and again...).\n\nOr just iterate over the map and removes the least used one, it\u0027s just 10000 elements so should be finished in 1ms\n\nThis way, your code (e.g. refreshMfcInactiveDuration) will be largely simplified.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 747,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 747,
        "endChar": 77
      },
      "revId": "4b47131260c1f356f5aaeedbd757761f60a75e6d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
